{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said.</b> You should reflect that the entire passage is under the name Elohim, but here the specific Name — which is the attribute of mercy — began, because He is now about to promise that He will have mercy upon His people and deliver them through the attribute of mercy." "<b>I have surely seen.</b> In this verse there are three levels, one above the other: seeing, hearing, knowing. Above seeing is hearing, for the power of hearing is purer and subtler than the power of seeing. Above both of them is knowing, for the completion of seeing or hearing is only through knowing: if a person sees something or hears a sound but does not know what it is, it is as though he did not see that thing or did not hear that sound. And therefore these two faculties come in the Torah in place of understanding — hearing, as it is written (Deuteronomy 28:49): ״גוי אשר לא תשמע לשונו״; seeing, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 1:16): ״ולבי ראה״. And one who knows a thing, even though he has never seen it or heard it, it is as though he saw it or heard it." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ראה ראיתי״ — two seeings; why? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: Moses, you see one seeing and I see two seeings — you see them coming to Sinai and receiving the Torah, and I see how they gaze upon Me and pluck one of My tetramorphs, as it is said (Ezekiel 1:10): ״ופני שור מהשמאל״, and thereby provoke Me."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "Reading שומטין as 'they pluck/tear away,' referring to Israel casting the image of the ox (the cherub-face) into rebellion (e.g., the golden calf). The precise form שומטין is textually unusual; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:40.640060236Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}